 "description": "Count from one to a hundred and ask how much things cost.",
 "grammar_note": {
  "title": "Two readings, one number",
  "body": "Most numbers have one common reading: いち(1), に(2), さん(3)… but 4 and 7 have two: 4 = よん or し, 7 = なな or しち. In daily life よん and なな are safer because し also means 'death' (死). 100 is ひゃく and 1000 is せん."
 },
 "culture_note": "Prices in Japan are often shown without tax (税抜 zeinuki). When shopping you'll constantly hear 〜えん (yen): せんえん = 1000 yen. The number 4 (し) is considered unlucky — many hospitals skip room number 4!",
